The Go code in this directory and its subdirectories is a port of parts of
these JavaScript packages, in the versions that mermaid 12.2.0 bundles:

  cytoscape 3.34.0                https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape.js
  cytoscape-cose-bilkent 4.1.0    https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape.js-cose-bilkent
  cytoscape-fcose 2.2.0           https://github.com/iVis-at-Bilkent/cytoscape.js-fcose
  cose-base 1.0.3 and 2.2.0       https://github.com/iVis-at-Bilkent/cose-base
  layout-base 1.0.2 and 2.0.1     https://github.com/iVis-at-Bilkent/layout-base

All of them have the MIT license. The license texts and the copyright
notices of the packages are in the file LICENSES.txt of the parent directory
(internal/cytoscape). The port is a derivative work of the packages. Each
ported file names the source file, the package and the version that it was
ported from.

The file fcose/svd.go is a port of src/util/SVD.js of layout-base 2.0.1,
whose singular value decomposition is adopted from JamaJS
(https://github.com/dragonfly-ai/JamaJS), which has the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). layout-base
changed that code to take a two-dimensional array and to return an object
with the components, and the port changed it to Go.

The files cosebilkent.go and architecture.go also port the statements of
mermaid 12.2.0 (https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid, MIT license) that
create the cytoscape instance and read its results, as the other packages of
this module port mermaid.

The golden files in testdata are records of the behavior of the packages in
the JavaScript interpreter of internal/cytoscape.
